  "evidences": [
    {
      "id": "ev_1",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Proofpoint_Russia-Aligned-TA499-Beleaguers-Targets-Video-Call-Requests(03-07-2023)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "executive_summary",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s1"
      },
      "text": "TA499, also known as Vovan and Lexus, is a Russia-aligned threat actor that has aggressively engaged in email campaigns since at least 2021.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_2",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Proofpoint_Russia-Aligned-TA499-Beleaguers-Targets-Video-Call-Requests(03-07-2023)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "executive_summary",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s2"
      },
      "text": "The threat actor’s campaigns attempt to convince high-profile North American and European government officials as well as CEOs of prominent companies and celebrities into participating in recorded phone calls or video chats.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_4",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Proofpoint_Russia-Aligned-TA499-Beleaguers-Targets-Video-Call-Requests(03-07-2023)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s4"
      },
      "text": "Russia-Aligned TA499 Beleaguers Targets with Video Call Requests Proofpoint researchers have been tracking malicious email campaigns by the Russia-aligned TA499, publicly known as Vovan and Lexus, since early 2021.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_10",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Proofpoint_Russia-Aligned-TA499-Beleaguers-Targets-Video-Call-Requests(03-07-2023)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s1"
      },
      "text": "While the level of official government support TA499 receives is unknown, the recordings are generally used to garner support and sympathy for the current Russian regime and their actions.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_12",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Proofpoint_Russia-Aligned-TA499-Beleaguers-Targets-Video-Call-Requests(03-07-2023)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s3"
      },
      "text": "Since late-January 2022, the threat actor has largely focused its email attempts on scheduling a video or phone call meeting with high-profile North American or European government officials and CEOs of prominent companies.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_16",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Proofpoint_Russia-Aligned-TA499-Beleaguers-Targets-Video-Call-Requests(03-07-2023)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s7"
      },
      "text": "Early 2022: TA499’s initial 2022 campaigns used the same actor-controlled domain (oleksandrmerezhko[.]com) and sender address (office@oleksandrmerezhko[.]com) as its 2021 campaigns, and directly targeted individuals that had spoken out regarding:",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_19",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Proofpoint_Russia-Aligned-TA499-Beleaguers-Targets-Video-Call-Requests(03-07-2023)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s3"
      },
      "text": "To make the emails convincing in their legitimacy, the sender addresses leveraged the popular internet service and email provider Ukr.net and pretended to be from either “the Embassy of Ukraine to the US” or “the Embassy of Ukraine in the US:” embassy.usa@ukr[.]net and embassy.us@ukr[.]net.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_25",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Proofpoint_Russia-Aligned-TA499-Beleaguers-Targets-Video-Call-Requests(03-07-2023)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s3"
      },
      "text": "Mid-2022: By mid-2022, TA499 started to explore using an additional embassy-themed email address (embassy.chernysh@ukr[.]net) and even utilized an actor-controlled International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA)-themed domain (office@iaea[.]co[.]uk) to send emails with a subject line of “URGENT: IAEA Director General” to international aides and assistance of senior government officials.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_26",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Proofpoint_Russia-Aligned-TA499-Beleaguers-Targets-Video-Call-Requests(03-07-2023)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s4"
      },
      "text": "It is likely that the international attention surrounding the state of the power plant inspired TA499’s decision to use an IAEA lure.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_28",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Proofpoint_Russia-Aligned-TA499-Beleaguers-Targets-Video-Call-Requests(03-07-2023)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 5,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p5_s1"
      },
      "text": "Through the rest of 2022, TA499 integrated email addresses not observed in Proofpoint data since at least March 2022, including those pretending to be Oleksandr Merezhko, a Ukrainian Member of Parliament (MP) and Vice President of the Parliamentary Assembly of the Council of Europe (PACE), and Leonid Volkov, the Chief of Staff for Russian opposition leader Alexei Navalny (noted in Figure 2).",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_40",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Proofpoint_Russia-Aligned-TA499-Beleaguers-Targets-Video-Call-Requests(03-07-2023)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 8,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p8_s1"
      },
      "text": "Conclusion TA499 is a very public group that is garnering a fan following.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
